// ------------------------------------------------------------
//  Rozdział czternasty — Kapliczki płoną. Lato po wspólnym śnie (Marysia
//  kończy w sierpniu dwa lata). Paliki pod drogę Urbaniaka puszczają pędy,
//  bór podchodzi pod miedze. Szarwark z zeszytu długów: sprzeciw (krowa),
//  robota na przesiece (srebro, parobek z kaleką nogą, żywica na dłoni) albo
//  paliki w bagnie (Antek w areszcie, korale Jadwisi). W noc pożaru płoną
//  kapliczki i tartak, w stróżówce zaparty Szymon, ojciec Józka: ratować
//  kapliczkę, Szymona albo — gdy ubożę ostrzegło — zbudzić wieś (spalone dłonie).
//  Rano bór przychodzi o całe pole; Urbaniak spali zeszyt za drogę do boru.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

=== rozdzial_czternasty ===
# tlo: paliki_pedy
# rozdzial: Chapter Fourteen
# tytul: The Shrines Burn
At dawn Urbaniak’s men tore the green shoots off the stakes, and by the next day fresh ones bristled in the same places. After a week the foreman from the sawmill had new pegs driven into the ground—of oak, stripped of bark and dried by the stove. They lasted three days. On the fourth morning a sprig grew from every one of them, thin and sticky with resin, though oak has no resin. # pokaz: pedy
The summer came in hot and dry. Hay cured in the swathes in a single day, and the buckets had to be let down lower and lower into the wells. Marysia ran about the whole farmyard by now and chattered without pause, jumbling her words in her own way{ ekwipunek ? szczenie_psa:, while the big russet dog slept in the shade under the cart, always lying so that he could see where she had gone}. {trzy_noce == czuwanie_przy_kolysce:Of the Wójciks’ cottage only the walls were left now; the neighbours had pulled the roof apart for kindling.|Mrs Wójcik came to see her every Sunday with dried apples and sat on the threshold to watch the little one chase the hens.} Antek carried his Franek in his arms all over the village and showed everyone that the boy could already hold up his head by himself.
Only the woods would not let them be. The first to notice was {trzy_noce == czuwanie_przy_kolysce:Józek’s mother|Mrs Wójcik}: the field balk between her strip and the forest, always as wide as two carts, had one morning narrowed by half. Along it stood a row of young spruces, waist-high to a man, straight, as if planted to a line. No one had planted them. The men cut them down that same day, and a week later others stood in their place—taller. # pokaz: swierki # dalej
