# tlo: pogorzelisko
~ zapiski += pan_lasu_6
By morning the fire had died down, and people stood in silence on the burnt ground where the sawmill had been.
The forest had come up to the village. Not by a step or two—by a whole field. Where the day before the Wójciks’ stubble and the pasture at Staś’s had stretched, a dense wood now rustled, dewy and dark, with pale shoots at the tops of the trees, as though it had stood there for generations. {noc_ognia == ratowal_szymona:The ashes of the shrine by the cutting lay|The shrine by the cutting stood} in the middle of that young wood like a gravestone. # pokaz: las
{ los_figurki == figurka_pod_kapliczka:
    Jaromir went to the shrine under which he had buried the figurine in the spring. It had burned along with the others. The earth beneath it was cracked and wet, as after a downpour, though not a drop of rain had fallen.
}
Urbaniak came before noon, pale, the debt book in his hand. He walked round the burnt ground, then stopped in front of the people.
“Someone set fire to my property,” he said quietly. “And one of your people barred the door of the watchman’s hut.” He looked round at their faces. “I shan’t go looking for who. I’m offering you a bargain. By winter you take the road right up to the forest, just as it was marked out, and the timber you fell along it you cart to me in Bukowiec. Then I’ll burn this debt book before your eyes. Every debt, with interest, to the last grosz. And if not—I’ll send the bailiff, and he’ll take whatever he can from your byres.”
People looked at Jaromir. {noc_ognia == ratowal_kapliczke:Since the night of the fire, when he had fought the flames on the last shrine with his bare hands, the men listened to him as to an elder.|Ever since he had carried Szymon out of the fire, Józek’s mother would kiss his {noc_ognia == zbudzil_wies:sleeves|hands} in the lane, and the men had begun to listen to him as to an elder.}{ szarwark == robota_na_przesiece: Even those who in July had spat at his feet for working for Urbaniak.} Hanka stepped up beside him and took his arm—firmly, so that everyone could see.
“Tell them what you think,” she whispered. “But say what you yourself think, not what they want to hear.”
# pytanie: What will Jaromir say?
