Marysia had turned two in August. In the evenings, when Hanka put her to bed, the little one hummed the same tune under her breath, over and over—short, sad, with one note that always broke off halfway. Hanka no longer asked where she had learned it. She only began to leave a pine splint burning in the room at night. # pokaz: luczywo
On the night of Christmas Eve, as they were coming back from Midnight Mass, all Zapadlina saw a cloud of sparks hang for a moment above the young wood by the forest—though no one had lit a fire there, and under the snow there was nothing to catch. It went out before anyone had time to cross himself. # pokaz: iskry # dalej
